#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3. Quantum Optimization with Qiskit patterns {#3-quantum-optimization-with-"
"qiskit-patterns}"
msgstr ""
"3. Quantum Optimization dengan Qiskit patterns {#3-quantum-optimization-"
"with-qiskit-patterns}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this how-to we will learn about Qiskit patterns and quantum approximate optimization. A Qiskit pattern is an intuitive, repeatable set of steps for implementing a quantum computing workflow:\n"
"![\"Qiskit function\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/qiskit-function.avif)\n"
"We will apply the patterns to the context of **combinatorial optimization** and show how to solve the **max-cut** problem using the **Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA)**, a hybrid (quantum-classical) iterative method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bagian ini kita akan belajar tentang Qiskit patterns dan quantum approximate optimization. Qiskit pattern adalah serangkaian langkah yang intuitif dan berulang untuk mengimplementasikan alur kerja komputasi kuantum:\n"
"![\"Qiskit function\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/qiskit-function.avif)\n"
"Kita akan menerapkan patterns tersebut dalam konteks **optimisasi kombinatorial** dan menunjukkan cara menyelesaikan masalah **Max-Cut** menggunakan **Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA)**, sebuah metode iteratif hibrida (kuantum-klasik).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this QAOA part is based on \"Part 1: Small-scale QAOA\" of the "
"[Quantum approximate optimization algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-"
"optimization-algorithm) tutorial. See the tutorial to learn how to scale it "
"up.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu dicatat bahwa bagian QAOA ini didasarkan pada \"Part 1: Small-scale "
"QAOA\" dari tutorial [Quantum approximate optimization "
"algorithm](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm). Lihat "
"tutorial tersebut untuk belajar cara mengembangkannya ke skala yang lebih "
"besar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3.1 (Small-scale) Qiskit pattern for optimization {#31-small-scale-qiskit-"
"pattern-for-optimization}"
msgstr ""
"3.1 Qiskit pattern untuk optimisasi (skala kecil) {#31-small-scale-qiskit-"
"pattern-for-optimization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This part will use a small-scale max-cut problem to illustrate the steps required to solve an optimization problem using a quantum computer.\n"
"The max-cut problem is an optimization problem that is hard to solve (more specifically, it is an NP-hard problem) with a number of different applications in clustering, network science, and statistical physics. This tutorial considers a graph of nodes connected by edges and aims to partition the nodes into two sets by \"cutting\" edges, such that the number of edges cut is maximized.\n"
"![\"Maxcut\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/maxcut.avif)\n"
"To give some context before mapping this problem to a quantum algorithm, you can better understand how the max-cut problem becomes a classical combinatorial optimization problem by first considering the minimization of a function $f(x)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini akan menggunakan masalah Max-Cut skala kecil untuk mengilustrasikan langkah-langkah yang diperlukan untuk menyelesaikan masalah optimisasi menggunakan komputer kuantum.\n"
"Masalah Max-Cut adalah masalah optimisasi yang sulit diselesaikan (lebih tepatnya, ini adalah masalah NP-hard) dengan berbagai aplikasi dalam clustering, ilmu jaringan, dan fisika statistik. Tutorial ini mempertimbangkan sebuah graf berisi node yang terhubung oleh edge, dan bertujuan untuk membagi node-node tersebut menjadi dua himpunan dengan \"memotong\" edge, sehingga jumlah edge yang dipotong dimaksimalkan.\n"
"![\"Maxcut\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/maxcut.avif)\n"
"Untuk memberi konteks sebelum memetakan masalah ini ke algoritma kuantum, kamu bisa lebih memahami bagaimana masalah Max-Cut menjadi masalah optimisasi kombinatorial klasik dengan terlebih dahulu mempertimbangkan minimisasi fungsi $f(x)$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}f(x),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}f(x),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the input $x$ is a vector whose components correspond to each node of "
"a graph.  Then, constrain each of these components to be either $0$ or $1$ "
"(which represent being included or not included in the cut). This small-"
"scale example case uses a graph with $n=5$ nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana input $x$ adalah vektor yang komponennya berkorespondensi dengan "
"setiap node dari graf. Kemudian, batasi setiap komponen tersebut agar "
"bernilai $0$ atau $1$ (yang merepresentasikan apakah node tersebut masuk "
"dalam potongan atau tidak). Contoh skala kecil ini menggunakan graf dengan "
"$n=5$ node.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You could write a function of a pair of nodes $i,j$ which indicates whether "
"the corresponding edge $(i,j)$ is in the cut. For example, the function $x_i"
" + x_j - 2 x_i x_j$ is 1 only if one of either $x_i$ or $x_j$ are 1 (which "
"means that the edge is in the cut) and zero otherwise. The problem of "
"maximizing the edges in the cut can be formulated as\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu bisa membuat fungsi dari sepasang node $i,j$ yang menunjukkan apakah "
"edge yang bersesuaian $(i,j)$ ada dalam potongan. Misalnya, fungsi $x_i + "
"x_j - 2 x_i x_j$ bernilai 1 hanya jika salah satu dari $x_i$ atau $x_j$ "
"bernilai 1 (yang berarti edge tersebut ada dalam potongan) dan nol dalam "
"kasus lain. Masalah memaksimalkan edge dalam potongan dapat diformulasikan "
"sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)} x_i + x_j - 2 x_i x_j,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)} x_i + x_j - 2 x_i x_j,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which can be rewritten as a minimization of the form\n"
msgstr "yang dapat ditulis ulang sebagai minimisasi dalam bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)}  2 x_i x_j - x_i - x_j.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n} \\sum_{(i,j)}  2 x_i x_j - x_i - x_j.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The minimum of $f(x)$ in this case is when the number of edges traversed by the cut is maximal. As you can see, there is nothing relating to quantum computing yet. You need to reformulate this problem into something that a quantum computer can understand.\n"
"Initialize your problem by creating a graph with $n=5$ nodes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Minimum dari $f(x)$ dalam kasus ini adalah ketika jumlah edge yang dilintasi potongan maksimal. Seperti yang bisa kamu lihat, belum ada kaitannya dengan komputasi kuantum sama sekali. Kamu perlu memformulasikan ulang masalah ini menjadi sesuatu yang bisa dipahami oleh komputer kuantum.\n"
"Inisialisasi masalah dengan membuat graf dengan $n=5$ node.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/extracted-"
"outputs/99e763fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/extracted-"
"outputs/99e763fe-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3.2 Step 1. Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#32-step-1-map-"
"classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"3.2 Langkah 1. Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#32-step-1-map-"
"classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first step of the pattern is to map the classical problem (graph) into "
"quantum **circuits** and **operators**. To do this, there are three main "
"steps to take:\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah pertama dari pattern adalah memetakan masalah klasik (graf) ke dalam"
" **Circuit** dan **operator** kuantum. Untuk melakukan ini, ada tiga langkah"
" utama:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Utilize a series of mathematical reformulations, to represent this problem "
"using the Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) problems "
"notation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan serangkaian reformulasi matematis untuk merepresentasikan masalah "
"ini menggunakan notasi masalah Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization "
"(QUBO).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Rewrite the optimization problem as a Hamiltonian for which the ground state"
" corresponds to the solution which minimizes the cost function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulis ulang masalah optimisasi sebagai Hamiltonian yang keadaan dasarnya "
"berkorespondensi dengan solusi yang meminimalkan fungsi biaya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a quantum circuit which will prepare the ground state of this "
"Hamiltonian via a process similar to quantum annealing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Buat Circuit kuantum yang akan mempersiapkan keadaan dasar Hamiltonian ini "
"melalui proses yang mirip dengan quantum annealing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** In the QAOA methodology, you ultimately want to have an operator "
"(**Hamiltonian**) that represents the **cost function** of our hybrid "
"algorithm, as well as a parametrized circuit (**Ansatz**) that represents "
"quantum states with candidate solutions to the problem. You can sample from "
"these candidate states and then evaluate them using the cost function.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Catatan:** Dalam metodologi QAOA, pada akhirnya kamu ingin memiliki "
"operator (**Hamiltonian**) yang merepresentasikan **fungsi biaya** dari "
"algoritma hibrida kita, serta sebuah sirkuit berparameter (**Ansatz**) yang "
"merepresentasikan keadaan kuantum dengan kandidat solusi masalah. Kamu bisa "
"mengambil sampel dari keadaan kandidat ini dan kemudian mengevaluasinya "
"menggunakan fungsi biaya.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Graph &rarr; optimization problem {#graph-optimization-problem}"
msgstr "Graf &rarr; masalah optimisasi {#graph-optimization-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first step of the mapping is a notation change, The following expresses "
"the problem in QUBO notation:\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah pertama dari pemetaan adalah perubahan notasi. Berikut ini "
"mengekspresikan masalah dalam notasi QUBO:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}x^T Q x,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{x\\in \\{0, 1\\}^n}x^T Q x,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $Q$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix of real numbers, $n$ corresponds to the "
"number of nodes in your graph, $x$ is the vector of binary variables "
"introduced above, and $x^T$ indicates the transpose of the vector $x$.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $Q$ adalah matriks berukuran $n\\times n$ berisi bilangan real, $n$ "
"berkorespondensi dengan jumlah node dalam graf, $x$ adalah vektor variabel "
"biner yang diperkenalkan sebelumnya, dan $x^T$ menunjukkan transpose dari "
"vektor $x$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optimization problem &rarr; Hamiltonian {#optimization-problem-hamiltonian}"
msgstr ""
"Masalah optimisasi &rarr; Hamiltonian {#optimization-problem-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can then reformulate the QUBO problem as a **Hamiltonian** (here, a "
"matrix that represents the energy of a system):\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu kemudian bisa memformulasikan ulang masalah QUBO sebagai "
"**Hamiltonian** (di sini, sebuah matriks yang merepresentasikan energi suatu"
" sistem):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_C=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i b_iZ_i.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_C=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}Z_iZ_j + \\sum_i b_iZ_i.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Reformulation steps from the QAOA problem to the Hamiltonian**\n"
msgstr "**Langkah-langkah reformulasi dari masalah QAOA ke Hamiltonian**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To demonstrate how the QAOA problem can be rewritten in this way, first "
"replace the binary variables $x_i$ to a new set of variables $z_i\\in\\{-1, "
"1\\}$ via\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menunjukkan bagaimana masalah QAOA dapat ditulis ulang dengan cara "
"ini, pertama-tama ganti variabel biner $x_i$ dengan sekumpulan variabel baru"
" $z_i\\in\\{-1, 1\\}$ melalui\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here you can see that if $x_i$ is $0$, then $z_i$ must be $1$. When the "
"$x_i$'s are substituted for the $z_i$'s in the optimization problem "
"($x^TQx$), an equivalent formulation can be obtained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kamu bisa melihat bahwa jika $x_i$ bernilai $0$, maka $z_i$ harus "
"bernilai $1$. Ketika $x_i$ disubstitusi dengan $z_i$ dalam masalah "
"optimisasi ($x^TQx$), formulasi yang ekuivalen dapat diperoleh.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x^TQx=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}x_ix_j \\\\ =\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}(1-z_i)(1-z_j) \\\\=\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}z_iz_j-\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})z_i + \\frac{n^2}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x^TQx=\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}x_ix_j \\\\ =\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}(1-z_i)(1-z_j) \\\\=\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}Q_{ij}z_iz_j-\\frac{1}{4}\\sum_{ij}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})z_i + \\frac{n^2}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now if we define $b_i=-\\sum_{j}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})$, remove the prefactor, and "
"the constant $n^2$ term, we arrive at the two equivalent formulations of the"
" same optimization problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang jika kita mendefinisikan $b_i=-\\sum_{j}(Q_{ij}+Q_{ji})$, menghapus"
" faktor awal, dan suku konstanta $n^2$, kita tiba pada dua formulasi yang "
"ekuivalen dari masalah optimisasi yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"min_{x\\in\\{0,1\\}^n} x^TQx\\Longleftrightarrow \\min_{z\\in\\{-1,1\\}^n}z^TQz + b^Tz\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"min_{x\\in\\{0,1\\}^n} x^TQx\\Longleftrightarrow \\min_{z\\in\\{-1,1\\}^n}z^TQz + b^Tz\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, $b$ depends on $Q$. Note that to obtain $z^TQz + b^Tz$ we dropped the "
"factor of 1/4 and a constant offset of $n^2$ which do not play a role in the"
" optimization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, $b$ bergantung pada $Q$. Perhatikan bahwa untuk mendapatkan $z^TQz "
"+ b^Tz$ kita menghilangkan faktor 1/4 dan offset konstanta $n^2$ yang tidak "
"berperan dalam optimisasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, to obtain a quantum formulation of the problem, promote the $z_i$ "
"variables to a Pauli $Z$ matrix, such as a $2\\times 2$ matrix of the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, untuk mendapatkan formulasi kuantum dari masalah tersebut, "
"promosikan variabel $z_i$ menjadi matriks Pauli $Z$, seperti matriks "
"berukuran $2\\times 2$ berbentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
" $$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
" $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you substitute these matrices in the optimization problem above, you "
"obtain the following Hamiltonian\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika kamu mensubstitusi matriks-matriks ini ke dalam masalah optimisasi di"
" atas, kamu mendapatkan Hamiltonian berikut\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Also recall that the $Z$ matrices are embedded in the quantum computer's "
"computational space, that is, a Hilbert space of size $2^n\\times 2^n$. "
"Therefore, you should understand terms such as $Z_iZ_j$ as the tensor "
"product $Z_i\\otimes Z_j$ embedded in the $2^n\\times 2^n$ Hilbert space. "
"For example, in a problem with five decision variables the term $Z_1Z_3$ is "
"understood to mean $I\\otimes Z_3\\otimes I\\otimes Z_1\\otimes I$ where $I$"
" is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix.*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Ingat juga bahwa matriks $Z$ tertanam dalam ruang komputasi komputer "
"kuantum, yaitu ruang Hilbert berukuran $2^n\\times 2^n$. Oleh karena itu, "
"kamu harus memahami suku-suku seperti $Z_iZ_j$ sebagai produk tensor "
"$Z_i\\otimes Z_j$ yang tertanam dalam ruang Hilbert berukuran $2^n\\times "
"2^n$. Misalnya, dalam masalah dengan lima variabel keputusan, suku $Z_1Z_3$ "
"dipahami sebagai $I\\otimes Z_3\\otimes I\\otimes Z_1\\otimes I$ di mana $I$"
" adalah matriks identitas berukuran $2\\times 2$.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This Hamiltonian is called the <b>cost function Hamiltonian</b>. It has the property that its ground state corresponds to the solution that <b>minimizes the cost function $f(x)$</b>.\n"
"Therefore, to solve your optimization problem you now need to prepare the ground state of $H_C$ (or a state with a high overlap with it) on the quantum computer. Then, sampling from this state will, with a high probability, yield the solution to $\\min~f(x)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hamiltonian ini disebut <b>Hamiltonian fungsi biaya</b>. Ia memiliki sifat bahwa keadaan dasarnya berkorespondensi dengan solusi yang <b>meminimalkan fungsi biaya $f(x)$</b>.\n"
"Oleh karena itu, untuk menyelesaikan masalah optimisasi kamu sekarang perlu mempersiapkan keadaan dasar $H_C$ (atau keadaan dengan tumpang tindih yang tinggi dengannya) di komputer kuantum. Kemudian, pengambilan sampel dari keadaan ini akan, dengan probabilitas tinggi, menghasilkan solusi untuk $\\min~f(x)$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian &rarr; quantum circuit {#hamiltonian-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Hamiltonian &rarr; Circuit kuantum {#hamiltonian-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hamiltonian $H_C$ contains the quantum definition of your problem. Now "
"you can create a quantum circuit that will help *sample* good solutions from"
" the quantum computer. The QAOA is inspired by quantum annealing and applies"
" alternating layers of operators in the quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hamiltonian $H_C$ berisi definisi kuantum dari masalah kamu. Sekarang kamu "
"bisa membuat Circuit kuantum yang akan membantu *mengambil sampel* solusi "
"yang baik dari komputer kuantum. QAOA terinspirasi dari quantum annealing "
"dan menerapkan lapisan-lapisan operator yang berselang-seling dalam Circuit "
"kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The general idea is to start in the ground state of a known system, "
"$H^{\\otimes n}|0\\rangle$ above, and then steer the system into the ground "
"state of the cost operator that you are interested in. This is done by "
"applying the operators $\\exp\\{-i\\gamma_k H_C\\}$ and $\\exp\\{-i\\beta_k "
"H_m\\}$ with angles $\\gamma_1,...,\\gamma_p$ and "
"$\\beta_1,...,\\beta_p~$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide umumnya adalah memulai dari keadaan dasar sistem yang diketahui, "
"$H^{\\otimes n}|0\\rangle$ di atas, kemudian mengarahkan sistem ke keadaan "
"dasar operator biaya yang diinginkan. Ini dilakukan dengan menerapkan "
"operator $\\exp\\{-i\\gamma_k H_C\\}$ dan $\\exp\\{-i\\beta_k H_m\\}$ dengan"
" sudut-sudut $\\gamma_1,...,\\gamma_p$ dan $\\beta_1,...,\\beta_p~$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The quantum circuit that you generate is **parametrized** by $\\gamma_i$ and $\\beta_i$, so you can try out different values of $\\gamma_i$ and $\\beta_i$ and sample from the resulting state.\n"
"![\"QAOA circuit diagram\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/circuit-diagram.svg)\n"
"In this case we will try an example with 1 QAOA layer that contains two parameters: $\\gamma_1$ and $\\beta_1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit kuantum yang kamu hasilkan **berparameter** oleh $\\gamma_i$ dan $\\beta_i$, sehingga kamu bisa mencoba berbagai nilai $\\gamma_i$ dan $\\beta_i$ dan mengambil sampel dari keadaan yang dihasilkan.\n"
"![\"QAOA circuit diagram\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/variational-quantum-algorithms/circuit-diagram.svg)\n"
"Dalam kasus ini kita akan mencoba contoh dengan 1 lapisan QAOA yang mengandung dua parameter: $\\gamma_1$ dan $\\beta_1$.\n"

